            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>The string-of-bombs is a beautiful yet explosive succulent that can be found as a dangerous passenger aboard many starships in the Pact Worlds. Native to the jungles of Castrovel, the string-of-bombs' explosive name comes from the softly glowing orange pods that dangle from their vines. These pods were developed as a defense mechanism against Castrovel's massive predators when thorns and vines proved insufficient deterrents.</p>\n<p>As the plant's explosive pods don't develop until full maturity, the string-of-bombs resembles other harmless succulents (including the closely related and harmless string-of-suns) and might be overlooked as low-maintenance ship greenery. Many gardeners remain unaware of the hazard they're cultivating until it literally blows up in their face.</p><hr /><h2>Infestations</h2><p>Invasive creatures plague Absalom Station and resist the most dedicated efforts to eliminate them. Whether lurking in the Ghost Levels or stowing away on starships, tenacious infestations are a constant problem in such a large and cosmopolitan station.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Starfinder Absalom Station"
            }
